        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: प्रतिपालयति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रतिपालयति — pratipālayati — \"keeps to; abides by\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि सः नियमं प्रतिपालयति, तर्हि सर्वे तं विश्वसन्ति। yadi saḥ niyamaṃ pratipālayati, tarhi sarve taṃ viśvasanti. If he keeps the rule, everyone trusts him."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः नियमं प्रतिपालितवान्, saḥ niyamaṃ pratipālitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रतिपालयति (pratipālayati) is built on prati and the root √pāl, \"to guard, to keep\", which also gives pālayati; MW gives pratipālayati as to protect, to keep, to observe, and to wait for (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
